{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations","id":313221,"title":"Constantine, Arrow and DC Universe as inspirations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-15T13:15:37-08:00","id":313221,"title":"Constantine, Arrow and DC Universe as inspirations","content":"Lately we got the <i>Constantine</i> TV series, and it looks really good. ( Or rather, really dark <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). As <i>Hellblazer</i> is <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/awakened-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">official comic book series inspiration</a> for <b>Mage</b>, I thought that separate topic for Constantine-verse is in order. Beside, I started to read the <i>Books of Magic</i> from Gaiman, also starting John as one of main characters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Last episode of TV series is based on first <i>Hellblazer</i> issue and putting Constantine in confrontation with Mnemoth, Great Demon of Hunger. <b>Mage</b> ST question is this: <b>Is Mnemoth more Rank 4-6 Shadow Spirit or rather powerful Inferno Gluttony demon?</b> And TV series has nice way of handling the spirits ending existence/exorcism.<br /> <br /> And what would be the Manny, an authoritative angel? Empyrean one ( the Virtue spirit) ? Maybe a specific Unchained working for something other than God Machine? For Qashmallim he is a bit too human, I must agree. Maybe there is more in <i>Hellblazer</i> on him? I didn\u2019t see him in comics - but I read only few issues before, so I could just missed him.<br /> <br /> P.S. John Constantine is SSSSOOOO Mastigos! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T13:38:30-08:00","id":313260,"title":"","content":"I always wondered what kind of mage Constantine would be in both lines of mage. In awakening I can totally see him as a mastigos from the free council. Mastigos for two reasons, one he is an absolute bastard and two his magic works mostly around twisting people and demons minds and perceptions, manipulating and tricking them into doing exactly what he wants. Free council because as far as I can remember Constantine has never been one to follow orders, he's independent and does whatever the hell he wants. Ascension on the other hand is more difficult because I don't see him fitting in any of the traditions, perhaps among the hollow ones but I'm not sure. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T14:07:40-08:00","id":313287,"title":"","content":"He also uses numerous Sleeper occult practices in his magic, which is in the Free Council's wheelhouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T14:30:41-08:00","id":313301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=313260#post313260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In awakening I can totally see him as a mastigos from the free council.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Mastigos also goes he's other neat trick is teleportations, sympathy and &quot;travel magic&quot; - which he shows in <i>Books of Magic</i>, showing Tim's the world of magic - as much a Space as you could get.<br /> <br /> But to the Free Council I'm not as much convinced - he also is all days fighting the Darkness, actively seek and confront the Evil. I could say he could be from Adamantine Arrow also.<br /> <br /> And I don't get from character a vibe &quot;humanity is important&quot; or &quot;destroy the servants of Lie&quot; the rest of Libertines are known for...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-15-2014, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T14:54:46-08:00","id":313313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I don't get from character a vibe &quot;humanity is important&quot; or &quot;destroy the servants of Lie&quot;... </div> </div> </div>I do. He is usually messing up and sticking it up to demons and other supernatural forces that see humans as pocket money or pawns. There are no &quot;followers of the Lie&quot;, obviously, but you should see all the political critique and discourse that is in most of his stories. Demons cheering the re-election of Margaret Tatcher? You bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T16:09:04-08:00","id":313334,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in the sense that the Seers are followers of the Lie and they maintain the entrenched power structures that Constantine hates, he'd definitely want to destroy the servants of the Lie. He'd make for a very good, if very cynical, Invisible I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T17:55:16-08:00","id":313377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=313301#post313301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But to the Free Council I'm not as much convinced - he also is all days fighting the Darkness, actively seek and confront the Evil. I could say he could be from Adamantine Arrow also.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but I don't see that, constantine fights evil yes but many times he does it for purely selfish reasons and again I just don't see constantine subjecting himself to any kind of hierarchy taking into account how much he despises authority. He's more the kind of guy to have a network of contacts and allies but nothing else, the free council is perfect for how he operates because it usually works that way. Last but not least let's not forget that he is ultimately a pragmatist, he takes pieces of occult knowledge here and there. He doesn't follow any particular magical tradition he just takes what he thinks would be more useful. The free council is perfect to pick all kinds of different magical tricks and get help from many different types of awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T20:06:54-08:00","id":313446,"title":"","content":"I just can't get past the network straight-washing the character. I mean, I knew it was kind of inevitable, but that doesn't make me more ok with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T01:58:17-08:00","id":313569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=313446#post313446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just can't get past the network straight-washing the character. I mean, I knew it was kind of inevitable, but that doesn't make me more ok with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the last episode - &quot;Feast of Friends&quot; - I must say that both straight and smoke-washing is just in words. The last episode were really dark and some time disgusting. Constantine is trying to smoke in it, only the events don't let him. The relation with Gary is cleary cult-like fascination - I could easily see that Gary was Johns ex-boyfriend that would do anything for him.<br /> <br /> Beside, on Comic Con produces say that John <b>is</b> <a href=\"http://www.cinemablend.com/television/Constantine-Bisexual-Chainsmoker-Here-What-DC-Says-68002.html\" target=\"_blank\">bisexual in show</a>, only we won't see him &quot;jumping to other side&quot; on the beginning. They get the fans want &quot;real deal&quot;, only they won't dwell on that now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I would take issue with the presentation of Constantine through the run of the comics as a chain-smoking bisexual. He's been chain-smoking without a doubt, but this curious character aspect of him was revealed very late in the run. It might have been followed up once. It just wasn't a defining part of who he is. Could that exist in our universe? Sure. Look, we are following the course of the comic. I don\u2019t mean this as a cop-out at all. The comic ran for a very long time, presenting a character and building out this character, who was different with many passions and conflicts and torments and tragedies. That's what we're hanging our stories on.</div><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">So don\u2019t expect John Constantine to have a line of hot Latin male lovers right out the gate (obviously), but at least they\u2019re not immediately ruling out the possibility that his \u201ccurious character aspect\u201d will be introduced. I won\u2019t be surprised if, four years later, the show still hasn\u2019t made even passing mention of Constantine\u2019s flippant libido, but at least they weren\u2019t verbally against it from the beginning. Is that a victory here? Probably not. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>In comic books he was like, what, 2 years from the start of the series shown with his first male lover? I can live with that, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-16-2014, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T02:31:33-08:00","id":313577,"title":"","content":"Back to the topic - if we mostly agree on Johns &quot;<b>Awakening</b> version&quot; ( I won't defend Adamantine Arrow angel, as it was more &quot;it could be&quot; in my mind ), maybe we should explore a whole <a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/The_Trenchcoat_Brigade_(group)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Trenchcoat Brigade</b></a> squad? They also makes very interesting cabal model, even if very un<b>Mage</b> one in my POV.<br /> <br /> So, Brigade is consistence in <b>Awakening</b> with:<ul><li><u><a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/John_Constantine\" target=\"_blank\">John Constantine</a></u> - Free Council Mastigos wanting to get away with his contract he signed on his Awakening with one of Pandemonium's ( or maybe Inferno's? ) demons</li> <li><u><a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/The_Phantom_Stranger\" target=\"_blank\">The Phantom Stranger</a></u> - I will make here a bit a big guess, but Unchained Demon ( i.e. Fallen Angel ) could interesting. Maybe a Psychopomp Inquisitor?</li> <li><u><a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Doctor_Occult\" target=\"_blank\">Doctor Occult</a></u> - Acanthus Mysterium mage, sharing body with his other persona and a lover, <a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Rose_Psychic\" target=\"_blank\">Rose Psychic</a>.</li> <li><u><a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Mister_E\" target=\"_blank\">Mister E</a></u> - Obrimos Banisher ( or typical &quot;monster hunter&quot; ) with large affinity for Time Arcanum and large mental problems.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-05-2014, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T04:57:08-08:00","id":313610,"title":"","content":"Fun fact - Doctor Occult / Rose is why second edition points out that mages can look and act <i>very</i> different when in the Astral Realms, as their soul's self-image does not necessarily match their physical bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T06:18:08-08:00","id":313629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=313610#post313610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact - Doctor Occult / Rose is why second edition points out that mages can look and act <i>very</i> different when in the Astral Realms, as their soul's self-image does not necessarily match their physical bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mages souls can also be splinted in two in Astral?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T07:06:00-08:00","id":313666,"title":"","content":"What we know is that a male-looking mage in the physical plane can look as female in the Astral, for example. Or younger, or older, or from a different etnicity even, who knows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T10:11:23-08:00","id":313833,"title":"","content":"Having read the comic, I'd say John would be a lot of fun as a Mastigos or Thyrsus. The TV show was greatly disappointing in many ways but it did have some pretty strong Awakening themes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T10:16:37-08:00","id":313834,"title":"","content":"What would Zed from the TV show be in nWod terms (I have only passing familiarity with the comic)? Is she just a regular WOD human, with some supernatural psychic merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T10:22:02-08:00","id":313835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=313834#post313834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is she just a regular WOD human, with some supernatural psychic merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Best would be, probably, Proximi with some minor Time Arcanum - like 2nd dot - powers. She has couple of powers connected to Time, so a bit above from normal &quot;psychics&quot; that, typically, have only one, maybe two of them. And if I remember comics, she become lesser sorceress herself, so Proximi could be good for her. Plus, she totally don't freak out on Constantine's magic, so it could be her inner Sleepwalker status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T13:24:48-08:00","id":313925,"title":"","content":"what about his refuge? how would you put it in merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T13:46:04-08:00","id":313935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=313925#post313925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what about his refuge? how would you put it in merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't it be just Sanctum with very high security? In <b>Mage</b> 2ed Sanctum Merit is &quot;overlay&quot; on general Safehouse, adding only bonuses to spellcasting. High security in <b>Mage</b> can mean &quot;non gravity traps&quot; or &quot;endless labirynths&quot; inside Sanctums. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T03:15:12-08:00","id":318834,"title":"","content":"Latest episode very interesting. Especially in the light of coming 2 ed. If you didn't watch it, see now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For the rest of us see in spoiler.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Papa Midnite is sssoooo <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/death-is-the-road-to-awe/\" target=\"_blank\">new Moros</a>. He is respectful for the dead, but also getting humans to confront with transformation of the end of they life. He is materialistic, sure, but also humanitarian. Also his clashes in the episode with Constantine on the traditions of magic were very interesting to see, as Constantine would be Free Council member. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Other question: Beside Papa Midnite being Moros, what Order you would ascribe to him? Silver Ladder, because his working for greater force? Mysterium for his dedication to older tradition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T05:26:49-08:00","id":318875,"title":"","content":"He seems to be working for himself entirely, so not Silver Ladder, and he is only peripherally concerned with getting more knowledge from what I've seen. His main gist would be money, power, control. Maybe not even an order in his case? His demeanor does fit for a SL-guy though, I have to admit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T06:22:49-08:00","id":320651,"title":"","content":"<b>NBC is halting production of second season of TV series!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When the series is getting better and better with each episode... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you are concerned with the <i>Constantine</i>, please <b>#SaveConstantine</b>, and <b><a href=\"http://www.ipetitions.com/petition/save-constantine\" target=\"_blank\">sign the petition</a></b> for the renewal for second season.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T10:13:49-08:00","id":320867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=320651#post320651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>NBC is halting production of second season of TV series!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When the series is getting better and better with each episode... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you are concerned with the <i>Constantine</i>, please <b>#SaveConstantine</b>, and <b><a href=\"http://www.ipetitions.com/petition/save-constantine\" target=\"_blank\">sign the petition</a></b> for the renewal for second season.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is my understanding that NBC simply decided not to order additional episodes of Season 1, other than the 13 originally planned, and that no decision at all has been made about a second season.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T20:40:25-08:00","id":321352,"title":"","content":"Not ordering more episodes <b>is</b> a bad sign... Even if series go better and better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T11:25:58-08:00","id":331346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=313577#post313577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Brigade is consistence in <b>Awakening</b> with:<ul><li><u><a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/John_Constantine\" target=\"_blank\">John Constantine</a></u> - Free Council Mastigos wanting to get away with his contract he signed on his Awakening with one of Pandemonium's ( or maybe Inferno's? ) demons</li> <li><u><a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/The_Phantom_Stranger\" target=\"_blank\">The Phantom Stranger</a></u> - I will make here a bit a big guess, but Unchained Demon ( i.e. Fallen Angel ) could interesting. Maybe a Psychopomp Inquisitor?</li> <li><u><a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Doctor_Occult\" target=\"_blank\">Doctor Occult</a></u> - Acanthus Mysterium mage, sharing body with his other persona and a lover, <a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Rose_Psychic\" target=\"_blank\">Rose Psychic</a>.</li> <li><u><a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Mister_E\" target=\"_blank\">Mister E</a></u> - Obrimos Banisher ( or typical &quot;monster hunter&quot; ) with large affinity for Time Arcanum and large mental problems.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I read more of the <i>Books of Magic </i>series and I can have interesting idea for Tim...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Timothy_Hunter\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Timothy &quot;Tim&quot; Hunter</b></a> - Tim is Acanthus, probably Mysterium, but could be Silver Ladder. He is convinced that is both son of mortal sorcerer Tamlin and fae queen Titania from Arcadia, or his earth mother and father. And many other possibilities of origins, as <b>the</b> Merlin ( yes, Dark Ages Archmaster one ) cast him to be his successor in modern times, erasing part of Tims own reality - his beginning - in the process. In <b>Awakening</b> he could be Morovan's heir. Or maybe he <b>is</b> Morovan's true identity? Or other reality version of him? Ach, Acanthus Path...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-05-2014, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T12:05:07-08:00","id":331371,"title":"","content":"Could the justice league dark exist in Awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T21:22:05-08:00","id":331891,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not.<br /> <br /> Frankenstein's Monster canonically exists in both DC and the Promethean game (Verney).<br /> Deadman could either be a Moros or possibly a Sin-Eater. (Or just a curiously potent and self-aware ghost.)<br /> Madame Xanadu is, naturally, VERY Acanthus with her divinations and whatnot.<br /> Zatanna...not entirely sure which path she would be. Could be Acanthus, Mastigos or go classical wizard Obrimos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T00:58:29-08:00","id":332024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=331891#post331891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zatanna...not entirely sure which path she would be. Could be Acanthus, Mastigos or go classical wizard Obrimos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I use mine own idea, but I would make her the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/245242-magicians-and-awakened?p=293342#post293342\">Illusionist of Truth</a> - this Mastigos Legacy was based on idea the<b> Zatanna</b> and many other wizards used in pop culture - to &quot;Hide in the Plain Sight&quot;, as stage magician. Still, not sure if more Silver Ladder or Free Council mage here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T07:47:05-08:00","id":339994,"title":"","content":"So, in latest episode we have very interesting plot development I will not talk here. But I would like to say about a thing character do in it - a bi-location, being in to place at once. In <b>Mage</b>, would it be a Space spell, or maybe kind of Astral Projection from Mind? Also, a very interesting of usage Portal in Sanctum's defence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T08:32:15-08:00","id":340052,"title":"","content":"Actually existing in two places at once is indeed a Space effect. Projecting your conscious mind into Twilight is a Mind spell, and leaves your body vulnerable unless you take the precaution of being in a secured sanctum when you do so.<br /> <br /> Making someone <i>think</i> that you are somewhere when in fact you're someplace else could also be accomplished with either Mind (hallucination) or Prime (illusion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T21:04:16-08:00","id":340462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=340052#post340052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually existing in two places at once is indeed a Space effect. Projecting your conscious mind into Twilight is a Mind spell, and leaves your body vulnerable unless you take the precaution of being in a secured sanctum when you do so.<br /> <br /> Making someone <i>think</i> that you are somewhere when in fact you're someplace else could also be accomplished with either Mind (hallucination) or Prime (illusion).</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I believe Prime isn't illusion anymore, instead being about creating more &quot;real&quot; versions of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T12:31:27-08:00","id":381256,"title":"","content":"First warning for TV series - Felix Faust should be weak apprentice possessed by ancient Ghost Mage, not a old men Tremere... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T13:06:21-08:00","id":381297,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to create a Death spell such as the one John cast on Chas? Say, you slay X people and convert them into extra lives?<br /> <br /> That would make for a cool Reaper Legacy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T07:53:05-08:00","id":381974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=381297#post381297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible to create a Death spell such as the one John cast on Chas? Say, you slay X people and convert them into extra lives?<br /> <br /> That would make for a cool Reaper Legacy</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it's possible to do something like that... The broad outlines of such a power exist in the setting already, in the Geist self-ressurection, when they take over someone else's body.<br /> <br /> Sure, it'd be stepping on the toes of another Splat, but if it's just for a doggedly persistent villain, it could be a cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T05:17:45-08:00","id":388336,"title":"","content":"Watched Fridays &quot;A Whole World Out There&quot; - it's a nice Astral Realms story. Beside the Mad Mastigos that linger in Temenos Realm outside of his own death, there is weird &quot;power-level&quot; glitch. I always assumed that friends of John, the Newcastle Crew, were all Sleepwalkers with lesser supernatural Merits. But suddenly Ritchie is master of Astral creation, not the John that is proper magus - what is that? Not too mentioned <a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Ritchie_Simpson\" target=\"_blank\">Ritchie in comics is quantum mage</a>, that is more based on probability, than travels to inner mind.<br /> <br /> As <b>Mage</b> game question - how large would be on Mind this spell to create this kind of Domain for Awakened to linger after?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T06:30:59-08:00","id":388374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not too mentioned Ritchie in comics is quantum mage, that is more based on probability, than travels to inner mind.</div> </div> </div> </div> How could you say that on the same line with a link to a wiki that explains how Ritchie is actually quite capable at traveling the astral/digital planes and in fact is one of the best at doing so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T11:54:20-08:00","id":397864,"title":"","content":"Good news, everyone! <a href=\"http://screenrant.com/constantine-moving-to-syfy-hellblazer/\" target=\"_blank\">Constantine TV show is probably going to the SyFy channel</a> to become even edgier &quot;Hellblazer&quot;! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T12:35:51-08:00","id":397900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=397864#post397864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the SyFy channel</div> </div> </div> </div>Last year I probably wouldn't have been impressed, but their Helix series is pretty good. I just hope it doesn't sour NBC on DC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T23:55:06-08:00","id":423882,"title":"","content":"Getting the hook: which path do you see both Constantine (comic version) and his &quot;brother&quot; (the laughing magician) ?<br /> <br /> For Constantine, I believe he is a Mastigos with a dash of Fate, while his brother an Acanthus with Prime. What do you say?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:42:14-08:00","id":424298,"title":"","content":"&quot;Virtue: Fortitude<br /> Vice: Lust&quot;<br /> <br /> I know he likes the ladies, and supposedly some of the men, but I would put the cocky bastards vice as Pride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:26:46-08:00","id":424322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=424298#post424298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Virtue: Fortitude<br /> Vice: Lust&quot;<br /> <br /> I know he likes the ladies, and supposedly some of the men, but I would put the cocky bastards vice as Pride.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vice-Ridden, perhaps?<br /> <br /> But yeah, Pride is his #1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T19:11:48-07:00","id":694435,"title":"","content":"As you probably know - <a href=\"http://www.ew.com/article/2015/08/11/arrow-matt-ryan-constantine\" target=\"_blank\">Constantine will be guestly in <i>Arrow</i>, in fifth episode of today started fourth</a>. What's even more shocking, <i>Arrow</i> just started it's season and went all the way in to <b>Mage</b> territory. Just see this fighting scene with <i>Damian Darhk</i> from episode S04E01...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IQgn67rZMZc\" data-code=\"IQgn67rZMZc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/IQgn67rZMZc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> What would be those effects in your thinking? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-09-2015, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T00:01:49-07:00","id":694609,"title":"","content":"0:50 Forces Fraying, possibly Unravelling<br /> Life Perfecting to boost Strength so 1:11 happens<br /> 1:26 Life Unravelling<br /> Forces Veiling or Space Patterning to vanish, probably with Fate 2 to make it conditional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T01:23:58-07:00","id":694667,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://dc.wikia.com/wiki/Atlantis\" target=\"_blank\">Atlantis version from DC</a> sounds a lot as Atlantean Orthodoxy of Mage coined by Silver Ladder with Mysterium. Just look...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DC Wikia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Although magic was the dominant means of power throughout the continent, noted intellectuals began to recognize the wisdom of science. While the rest of the world had yet to benefit from inventions such as the wheel, the Atlanteans were already developing highly advanced technological wonders. Legend has it that the Atlanteans even managed to combine science and sorcery to create the world's first space-craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, isn't it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T00:25:34-07:00","id":746029,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i><b>Moderators:</b></i> I would ask to change topic in to &quot;<b>Constantine &amp; Arrow ( Comic and TV series ) as inspiration</b>&quot; as it will be more suitable to now content of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br /> <br /> As dwelling more in to now developing occult background of <b>Arrow </b>series, let's see all the fuss over <a href=\"http://dc.wikia.com/wiki/Lazarus_Pit\" target=\"_blank\">Lasarus Pit</a> in the hands of <i>League of Assasins</i> from the season three and in full glory in season four.<br /> <br /> In <b>Arrow</b> ( and DC ) <i>Pit</i> can prolong your life, but it makes you &quot;wicked&quot;. Lately, it is shown it can even bring back the dead, only that the effects are more profound - and more you time being &quot;on the other side&quot;, the less human you return.<br /> <br /> So the rules are simple and mostly accurate with what 2ED Storytelling System is giving us ( <b>God Machine Rules Update</b>, page 41, for example ). Put simply, <b>using Lasarus Pit is stealing your soul</b>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Prolonging the life</b></span><br /> <br /> Character that use Pit to prolong his life is in the first stage of Soul Loss and get <b><i>Souless</i> Condition</b> - only diffrance is that does not have regaining Willpower throught Vice as Breaking Point. Lasarus Pit makes you &quot;wicked&quot; and driven by your Vice, but do not want you to become madman - <b>yet</b>. Instead, character have new Breaking Point on re-using the Pit - it can be years of between each one, but sooner or later the character need to re-use it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Bring back the dead</b></span><br /> <br /> If character was brought up from dead in number of days equal to her dots of Willpower, she gains <b><i>Enervated</i> Condition. </b>The difference from normal rules is that character can stop effects of this Condition by killing someone - it will make condition dormant for her Willpower dots in weeks. And each killing is Breaking Point for Integrity as always.<br /> <br /> If character was brought up from dead later than number of days in her Willpower dots, she gains <b><i>Thrall</i> Condition</b>. Unless soul restoring magic is performed, she will always be without a soul from now on.<br /> <br /> <b>Sum up</b><br /> <br /> So what do you think? Is it working with to date shown rules in <b>Arrow</b>? Is it working with 2ED Storytelling System?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-03-2015, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T12:08:45-08:00","id":751952,"title":"","content":"Constantine is hands down an acanthus-<br /> he rides what he calls the synchronicity wave- basically the series of coincidences that throw him into every plot, making him at the right place at the right time, every time. His mastery of fate magic helps him sniff out loopholes and make wild gambles on risky prospects that frequently throw his friends under the bus, and most of his greatest triumphs from the comic book series come from when he exploits the deals and arrangements that Heaven/Hell has to operate by- divining the specific bans that Spirits have, or noticing possible breaches of contracts way before they happen.<br /> <br /> Half the time most of his power comes from calling in favors that others owe him- ever wonder why they don't tell him to fuck off? It's cause he's got a kharma whammy bat if they do, hiding in his trenchcoat. Sure he has a bit of mind- to pull off the occasional jedi mind trick, but more often than not he's just along for the ride, relying on sheer luck(magic) to get him through. For further reference, He's referred to frequently as the Fool, embodying all the concepts of the tarot card that represents the Acanthus path, even being published on the fool's image in Vertigo's special edition of the tarot. He comes as one of the incarnations of his family line, The Constant One, a heritage of what's referred to as laughing magicians, magic workers who generate luck and trick others through oaths. John Constantine. Straight up Acanthus.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://volts48.deviantart.com/art/DB-Ghost-Rider-vs-John-Constantine-Prelude-546818093\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://existentialcomics.com/philosopher/Friedrich_Nietzsche\" target=\"_blank\">http://existentialcomics.com/philoso...rich_Nietzsche</a>","edited":{"userid":5537,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5537-spiderjerusalem","user":"spiderjerusalem","date":". 11-03-2015, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5537-spiderjerusalem","name":"spiderjerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T20:06:48-08:00","id":768902,"title":"","content":"I would rather stick with Constantine as Mastigos with Fate - he is so glorious bastard... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As the <a href=\"http://moviepilot.com/posts/3646171?lt_source=external,manual\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Universe movie is announced</a>, I want to maybe talk about mage-like characters from this production to come.<br /> Let's just start with...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://dc.wikia.com/wiki/Nimue_Inwudu_(New_Earth)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Madame Xanadu</b></a> - an immortal psychic and Tarot reader, Madame is Acanthus. With her take on manipulating other magician I would put her as Silver Ladder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T20:34:24-08:00","id":768916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=768902#post768902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather stick with Constantine as Mastigos with Fate - he is so glorious bastard... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As the <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://moviepilot.com/posts/3646171?lt_source=external,manual&quot;]Dark</a> Universe movie is announced[/URL], I want to maybe talk about mage-like characters from this production to come.<br /> Let's just start with...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://dc.wikia.com/wiki/Nimue_Inwudu_(New_Earth)&quot;]</a><b>Madame Xanadu</b>[/URL] - an immortal psychic and Tarot reader, Madame is Acanthus. With her take on manipulating other magician I would put her as Silver Ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? He isn't Mastigos by any definition. And you want to give hive Fate? It's your game I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T20:43:39-08:00","id":768920,"title":"","content":"I see him as Acanthus with Space, Prime, and Spirit. Magic circles, true names, knowledge if bans and pacts, etc. Smatterings of Death as well given his dealings with ghosts. (Note:im going by original Hellblazer only).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T21:52:30-08:00","id":768956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=768916#post768916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously? He isn't Mastigos by any definition. And you want to give hive Fate? It's your game I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Constatine is egotistical bastard wanting to get himself out of Soul Pack with demons, he, literally, sold to Hell - How this is <b>not</b> Mastigos?<br /> <br /> And Mastigos can have high Fate without being Masters - Adept is still high in Arcana level. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T01:00:30-08:00","id":769030,"title":"","content":"Probably because Mastigos are manipulative in a different way than Acanthus.<br /> <br /> Selling your soul? That's a contract, a contract is an Oath. Acanthus are about breaking bonds of consequences, Mastigos break the bonds of social conventions. It could go either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T02:51:23-08:00","id":769063,"title":"","content":"Following <a href=\"http://dc.wikia.com/wiki/John_Constantine_(New_Earth)\" target=\"_blank\">DC Wikia on Constantine</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DC Wikia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">John Constantine is an occult detective from Liverpool, England. His violent and anti-social attitude makes him a formidable anti-hero, and he's known for doing whatever it takes to get the job done.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/marvel_dc/images/5/56/Quote1.png/revision/latest?cb=20080808033149\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/marvel_dc/images/5/56/Quote1.png/revision/latest?cb=20080808033149\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a> I'll kick them in the bollocks and spit on them when they're down, and then I'll be gone back into the darkness, leaving only a nod and a wink and a wisecrack. <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/marvel_dc/images/8/88/Quote2.png/revision/latest?cb=20080808033200\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/marvel_dc/images/8/88/Quote2.png/revision/latest?cb=20080808033200\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div> </div> </div> </div>And <a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/John_Constantine\" target=\"_blank\">Hellblazer Wikia</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hellblazer Wikia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Characterization</b><br /> <br /> Although a compassionate humanist who struggles to overcome the influence of both Heaven and Hell over humanity and despite his occasional forays into heroism, Constantine is a foul-mouthed cynic who pursues a life of sorcery and danger. His motivation has been attributed to an adrenaline addiction that only the strange and mysterious can sate. He also seems to be something of a &quot;weirdness magnet&quot;.<br /> <br /> Constantine is shown to be someone with a wide and international circle of contacts and allies, and is supremely adept at making friends. He has had many girlfriends as well, and mentions past boyfriends in Hellblazer issue 51. However, a running theme in the book is that his close friends inevitably suffer or are outright killed simply by being in his life; this has left a severe mark on him. In Hellblazer issue 69, when The King of Vampires killed a man in front of John and casually asked if he'd been a friend, John replied &quot;Must be. He's dead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, it's sound as typical representative of Mastigos Path...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T04:23:06-08:00","id":769098,"title":"","content":"You can't give evidence without justification and then expect everyone to buy into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T04:36:46-08:00","id":769105,"title":"","content":"I quoted justification: <i>&quot;His violent and anti-social attitude makes him a formidable anti-hero, and he's known for doing whatever it takes to get the job done.&quot;</i> And <i>&quot;Although a compassionate humanist who struggles to overcome the influence of both Heaven and Hell over humanity and despite his occasional forays into heroism, Constantine is a foul-mouthed cynic who pursues a life of sorcery and danger. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> Plus adding whole thing with Hell in his backstory, clearly high Arcana of Space and Mind, and we have Mastigos character.<br /> <br /> Also, this event highlight that John would be from Path of Scourage:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hallblazer Wikia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of John's first acts of magic, as a child, was to hide all of his childhood innocence and vulnerability in a box to rid himself of it. (<a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Hellblazer_The_Books_of_Magic_issue_1\" target=\"_blank\">Hellblazer The Books of Magic issue 1</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-19-2015, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:27:15-08:00","id":769146,"title":"","content":"Well, according to Dave himself<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: [GMC WoD] How would you make John Constantine?</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Yeah - a mid-Gnosis, low-Arcana, surprisingly high Wisdom Mastigos.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":250,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","user":"Yuukale","date":". 11-19-2015, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:56:36-08:00","id":769243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/313221-constantine-arrow-and-dc-universe-as-inspirations?p=769105#post769105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I quoted justification: <i>&amp;quot;His violent and anti-social attitude makes him a formidable anti-hero, and he's known for doing whatever it takes to get the job done.&amp;quot;</i> And <i>&amp;quot;Although a compassionate humanist who struggles to overcome the influence of both Heaven and Hell over humanity and despite his occasional forays into heroism, Constantine is a foul-mouthed cynic who pursues a life of sorcery and danger. &amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> Plus adding whole thing with Hell in his backstory, clearly high Arcana of Space and Mind, and we have Mastigos character.<br /> <br /> Also, this event highlight that John would be from Path of Scourage:</div> </div> </div> </div>Hiding your innocence in a box is very Mastigos.<br /> <br /> Being a ruthless bastard who does whatever it takes to get the job done, being a cynic with flashes of humanism, anti-social, anti-heroic, struggling against powerful outside influences...that could be any Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T22:25:47-08:00","id":769779,"title":"","content":"More I have - Constantine is Mastigos Batman! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/F963uOF.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/tVsJqgH.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> It's from <b>Annual Books of Magic #3</b> ( 1999 ) and is non traditional canon - but it does make sense if you think about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned",